It's like orange and blue.

00:33:01.440 --> 00:33:05.700
You would need to know it was Knicks or, you know, I guess, like, the Celtics you can get

00:33:05.700 --> 00:33:07.860
away with just green. You would think that that's the Celtics.

00:33:07.980 --> 00:33:10.200
So, it's not like, it's not one shoe fits all.

00:33:10.340 --> 00:33:15.360
But, like, if you can only just do orange, I wouldn't assume if I'm playing the cab in New

00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:17.180
York City that it's like, yeah, those are my Knicks.

00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:20.180
Like, just think it's like, oh, these are just, that's Tyrone.

00:33:21.760 --> 00:33:29.060
That's Clemson. That's the same shoes. Now, what's funny about Tyrone is I've mentioned in the game there is the product placement

00:33:29.060 --> 00:33:30.260
of the British Knight sneaker.

00:33:30.400 --> 00:33:37.140
But Tyrone appears outside of this game as a character in the Power Team segments of the

00:33:37.140 --> 00:33:40.560
Video Power TV show, which I have never heard of.

00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:41.580
I don't even know what you're talking about.

00:33:41.760 --> 00:33:43.720
Yeah. Right. None of this makes any sense.

00:33:43.840 --> 00:33:49.260
But the Video Power TV show, the TV show hosted by Johnny Arcade.

00:33:49.500 --> 00:33:52.240
Hello. Sean's still not ringing any bells.

00:33:52.580 --> 00:33:53.400
Johnny Arcade.

00:33:53.760 --> 00:33:54.900
David Arquette.

00:33:55.160 --> 00:33:56.000
I have no idea.

00:33:56.340 --> 00:34:01.020
The cartoon show inside of the show, which was called The Power Team.

00:34:01.380 --> 00:34:07.040
It was a cartoon adventure featuring Johnny Arcade himself as a cartoon and a team of heroes

00:34:07.040 --> 00:34:11.820
from different NES games published by the publisher of this game, Acclaim.

00:34:11.820 --> 00:34:24.360
So, you had Max Force from Nark, Kuros from Wizards and Warriors, Quirk from a tomato from the game

00:34:24.360 --> 00:34:26.100
of the same name. I don't think we played Quirk.

00:34:26.340 --> 00:34:32.600
I don't think that any of this, like, there's absolutely no, like, name recognition in any

00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:35.400
of this. Well, you're not going to believe who I left out, though.

00:34:35.400 --> 00:34:38.020
Obviously, so Tyrone's in the game, in the show, too.

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:46.900
So, you have Tyrone, a basketball player, Quirk, a tomato, Max Force, a policeman, Kuros, a knight,

00:34:47.180 --> 00:34:49.180
and get ready for the big reveal.

00:34:49.740 --> 00:34:54.660
Bigfoot, that monster truck that we didn't know.

00:34:54.840 --> 00:34:57.100
It was a character? Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:34:57.380 --> 00:35:01.080
Bigfoot was a character on the show, which is, like, another form of product placement

00:35:01.080 --> 00:35:07.200
because Bigfoot was also, as we learned from Angry Fan Mail, that was a real monster truck

00:35:07.200 --> 00:35:08.640
that toured the United States.

00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:10.660
So, it seems like...

00:35:10.660 --> 00:35:15.780
I think, hold on. I would just like to clarify that I think that, like, we searched mid-episode and confirmed

00:35:15.780 --> 00:35:17.440
that it was a real monster truck.

00:35:17.560 --> 00:35:19.760
But, like, we just didn't know that at the beginning of the record.

00:35:19.880 --> 00:35:22.360
That's just how fast the fan mail gets to us, Sean.

00:35:23.300 --> 00:35:25.420
But, I need a clarification here.

00:35:25.640 --> 00:35:31.860
Was it the, like, was it the vehicle itself that was a character, or was the driver involved?

00:35:32.320 --> 00:35:34.000
Oh, yeah. Okay. It's the truck.

00:35:34.300 --> 00:35:40.520
So, it's a car, like, it's a car-style, sentient vehicle was a character on the show.

00:35:40.560 --> 00:35:42.000
I'm not saying it talked.

00:35:42.020 --> 00:35:43.340
I'm saying it's on the show.

00:35:45.480 --> 00:35:47.140
Okay. Just checking.

00:35:47.660 --> 00:35:49.340
But that's kind of weird, right, Tyrone?

00:35:49.340 --> 00:35:52.920
Like, is that even, like, an established character?

00:35:53.320 --> 00:35:55.100
I could understand Max Force.

00:35:55.300 --> 00:35:58.660
We said that that is such a great name on that episode.

00:35:58.840 --> 00:36:00.900
But, like, Tyrone?

00:36:01.500 --> 00:36:04.320
No last name Tyrone from Arch Rivals?

00:36:04.440 --> 00:36:07.120
Like, no way he's big enough to be in a cartoon with Bigfoot.

00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:28.760
I would try to think of another, like, analogy, but just by virtue of it being a nondescript, like, stand-in for any other professional basketball player, I can't think of another, like, generic character like that that would make it sound more ridiculous.

00:36:29.080 --> 00:36:30.180
So, yeah, no, it's strange.

00:36:30.180 --> 00:36:35.540
Who was the cool kid that we all played as in Micro Machines?

00:36:36.380 --> 00:36:39.820
Oh, yeah. What was his name?

00:36:40.520 --> 00:36:41.600
He had a cool name.

00:36:41.960 --> 00:36:44.020
Yeah, it was like Spike or something.

00:36:44.260 --> 00:36:45.300
Not Spike. Spider, Spider.

00:36:45.740 --> 00:36:49.440
Spider. It would be like if Spider had, like, a TV show.

00:36:49.660 --> 00:36:52.460
I don't know. Spider should be on a TV show.

00:36:52.460 --> 00:37:02.080
And I think Spider looks, and bear with me here, people, Spider does look like that guy who shows up in that one episode of Rugrats who's, like, really cool at DD's school.

00:37:02.560 --> 00:37:07.380
Yeah, he's just a greaser guy on a motorcycle, and he gives Tommy, like, a motorcycle helmet.

00:37:07.780 --> 00:37:13.240
Pretty cool. There's not much else.

00:37:13.380 --> 00:37:14.420
I think we covered a lot here.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:16.620
This is a good episode for just two people.

00:37:16.840 --> 00:37:22.620
38 minutes? Yeah, it's definitely a good idea to just say that it's a good episode.

00:37:23.600 --> 00:37:25.860
Yeah, that reinforces it in people's heads.

00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:28.180
They go, like, oh, yeah, this actually was a good episode.

00:37:28.280 --> 00:37:29.340
That was a good episode.

00:37:29.440 --> 00:37:30.560
I was really not enjoying it. Right, exactly.

00:37:30.700 --> 00:37:32.520
And then they realize, oh, I was enjoying it.

00:37:33.320 --> 00:37:37.420
Would you believe that this is only Midway's second ever basketball game?

00:37:38.020 --> 00:37:40.420
I'm surprised that it's not their first.

00:37:41.300 --> 00:37:49.750
Interesting. Their first was way back, way, way back in 1974 with the aptly titled TV Basketball.

00:37:50.580 --> 00:37:54.520
Well, it seems like they definitely took their time.

00:37:55.860 --> 00:37:57.240
Learning the ropes, yeah.

00:37:57.560 --> 00:38:01.900
But right after that, like, you know, again, like, we kind of mentioned this in the beginning,

00:38:02.040 --> 00:38:11.040
but this is not far away from NBA Jam, so they're getting very close to perfecting the formula here.

00:38:11.400 --> 00:38:18.540
Yeah, and basketball in 1974 anyway, like, not in real life, but, like, in a video game, it's like, what was that?

00:38:19.520 --> 00:38:23.620
I imagine that you had to put, like, a little cellophane thing over your TV.

00:38:24.020 --> 00:38:26.300
Right, to see the court, you know, lines.

00:38:27.380 --> 00:38:33.820
And to be fair, like, sometimes that's charming, but, like, I don't think I, like, I'm having a hard enough time with the sports games on the NES.

00:38:33.820 --> 00:38:35.520
I don't think I ever want to find out.

00:38:35.980 --> 00:38:37.700
Like, Pong? Great.

00:38:37.860 --> 00:38:41.140
That's every sports game to me before 1985.

00:38:42.140 --> 00:38:44.640
Every sports game before 1985 is just Pong.

00:38:48.620 --> 00:38:50.560
Okay, so we covered the show.

00:38:50.560 --> 00:38:53.460
We already said it was a great episode, so nobody can object to that.

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:57.020
Are there any other, like, definitive statements you'd like to make?

00:38:57.920 --> 00:39:02.360
The only definitive statement that I would like to make is that it's time for the Essential Games list.

00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:11.440
Well, there's a first time for everything, and by that I mean that's the first time Sean's ever called for the Essential Games list.

00:39:12.740 --> 00:39:14.740
Because it's the only way we can end the show, right?

00:39:14.740 --> 00:39:22.540
So I guess we have to wrap things up here, and I just want to say Arch Rivals should have been called Basket Brawl, first and foremost.

00:39:23.760 --> 00:39:25.400
Great little game here.

00:39:25.600 --> 00:39:28.000
One of the more fun basketball games that we've had.

00:39:28.220 --> 00:39:34.280
Not entirely sold on the, like, experience playing against computers.

00:39:35.080 --> 00:39:40.760
Not that the computers are, like, cheap or anything, but just it doesn't feel as fun as playing with another person.

00:39:41.540 --> 00:39:47.800
Another person's more likely to also just, like, accidentally fuck up as much as you do, and that's half the fun.

00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:51.300
I really do think that before this is a sports game, it's really a party game.

00:39:51.440 --> 00:39:53.240
It's not meant to be taken seriously.

00:39:55.360 --> 00:39:59.100
I enjoyed almost everything about the game, so I don't have too many complaints here.

00:39:59.220 --> 00:40:01.180
But it also just isn't full enough.

00:40:01.180 --> 00:40:06.320
And I think that's going to be a problem because, like, what does it mean to be full enough?

00:40:06.480 --> 00:40:12.620
But, like, Tecmo Bowl, which we did vote Essential, had, like, a lot going on.

00:40:12.820 --> 00:40:15.860
You know, granted, it was also just emulating football, right?

00:40:15.960 --> 00:40:17.520
Like, you would have to pick plays.

00:40:17.520 --> 00:40:19.860
You don't have to pick plays in basketball.

00:40:19.860 --> 00:40:24.060
But it just felt more complex and in-depth than what this is offering.

00:40:24.060 --> 00:40:31.040
I don't like a game where it's, like, most of the time I'm punching the air and just hoping it connects with my opponent.

00:40:31.180 --> 00:40:35.400
It is fun when it does connect, but it's not fun when it's not connecting.

00:40:35.580 --> 00:40:40.120
It is fun when I shatter the glass by doing an awesome dunk.

00:40:40.300 --> 00:40:43.860
It's not as much fun when I don't catch a rebound.

00:40:44.080 --> 00:40:48.380
The whole game is just kind of like an ebb and flow of, like, me deciding if I'm having enough fun.

00:40:48.460 --> 00:40:49.840
So that doesn't sound like fun.

00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:51.840
But it was fun.

00:40:51.860 --> 00:40:53.540
But it's not essential.

00:40:54.040 --> 00:40:55.800
Sean? Yeah.

00:40:56.740 --> 00:41:07.200
I'd say that in the roster of basketball games that we've played thus far, I think that this one at least has, like, the highest...

00:41:07.200 --> 00:41:16.440
I mean, not that you would genuinely or generally, like, think about, like, oh, what's the highest concept basketball game that we've played?

00:41:17.640 --> 00:41:21.360
This is the highest concept basketball game that we've played, I think.

00:41:21.980 --> 00:41:24.360
Like, we've had ones that are, like, half court.

00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:26.520
We've had ones that are five on five.

00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:31.680
We've had ones that are just literally two specific players playing against each other.

00:41:31.680 --> 00:41:43.260
Um, and I think that this is the one that if I had to play an 8-bit basketball game, I would choose to play this one.

00:41:43.900 --> 00:41:47.680
Um, that's not to say that this is essential, because it's not.

00:41:47.900 --> 00:41:57.260
But I think that this at least has enough unique qualities that it's the best one that we've played so far.

00:41:57.260 --> 00:42:11.140
Uh, and my historically terrible memory with video games that we've played on this show will at least keep this, uh, as something that I will remember.

00:42:11.440 --> 00:42:14.340
Maybe the title probably will make it hard.

00:42:14.520 --> 00:42:16.660
Like, what the hell does Arch Rivals mean?

00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:19.040
Right, right. But it's still a good game.

00:42:19.380 --> 00:42:23.940
Not essential, but, uh, one of the better sports games we've played so far.

00:42:23.940 --> 00:42:29.800
Uh, not that I disagree with your take on the whole, like, you know, best of basketball and everything.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:36.900
But I think, you know, listeners would, like, would, uh, most likely add in double dribble to that conversation.

00:42:36.940 --> 00:42:41.980
A game that, um, is beloved by many, uh, people who grew up with the NES.

00:42:42.280 --> 00:42:46.080
But it is also just sort of basketball.

00:42:46.380 --> 00:42:49.280
No, I agree. I guess I'm saying, like, I'm not siding with them.

00:42:49.420 --> 00:42:50.360
I'm siding with you.

00:42:50.360 --> 00:42:55.900
I'm saying, like, I actually do think Arch Rivals is more memorable at the end of the day.

00:42:56.040 --> 00:43:04.200
Double dribble is a competent basketball game on the NES, but I'd very quickly take 3D basketball over double dribble.

00:43:04.400 --> 00:43:05.440
Yeah, I agree.

00:43:05.460 --> 00:43:06.500
You know what I mean? I agree.

00:43:06.600 --> 00:43:07.900
That is exactly what I mean here.

00:43:08.140 --> 00:43:09.160
Right. Okay, cool.

00:43:09.740 --> 00:43:14.240
Uh, and, you know, would I say the same for almost any sports game?

00:43:14.320 --> 00:43:26.000
Yeah, sure. Like, I, I don't think, uh, even the great ones here, uh, RBI baseball, baseball stars, I don't think I'm ever picking those over the ones I grew up on.

00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:30.740
So I think there is always going to be, like, a nostalgia bias with sports games of, of toleration.

00:43:30.960 --> 00:43:32.020
You know what you tolerate.

00:43:32.600 --> 00:43:33.760
Toleration, yeah. Because, you know what I'm saying?

00:43:33.820 --> 00:43:34.740
Because you grew up with them.

00:43:34.840 --> 00:43:36.560
So it's like, yeah, I know the ins and outs of these.

00:43:36.560 --> 00:43:42.160
So I understand that, like, yeah, double dribble is way better than that, uh, Jordan vs.

00:43:42.240 --> 00:43:44.800
Bird game. Like, no one's, no one's denying that.

00:43:44.980 --> 00:43:52.300
But, like, it doesn't necessarily, like, deserve an essential title more than, like, Arch Rivals does.

00:43:52.300 --> 00:43:53.520
And neither one got it.

00:43:53.620 --> 00:43:54.440
So who really cares?

00:43:54.920 --> 00:43:56.340
Yeah, nothing matters.

00:43:57.400 --> 00:44:01.280
Uh, yeah. Do what you want, because it doesn't matter what you do.

00:44:02.240 --> 00:44:24.760
Do what you want, because it doesn't matter what you do.
